{
  "info": {
    "name": "NightOwl -- Day 3-13 API",
    "description": "Every NightOwl backend endpoint that exists through Pair 1's Day 13 milestone (Backend + Detection core + production hardening), plus Pair 2's Day 11 incident chat endpoint. Day 13 added shared-secret X-API-Key auth (every folder below except Health) and limit/offset pagination on GET /incidents -- set the api_key variable if your server has API_KEY configured, otherwise leave it blank. Import this alongside NightOwl.postman_environment.json and select the \"NightOwl Local\" environment. See docs/05_NightOwl_Manual_Testing_Guide.md Section 21 for the full step-by-step walkthrough, required setup per request, and expected responses, and Section 22.7 for the Day 13 auth/pagination/rate-limit walkthrough.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "incident_id",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "api_key",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No DB needed. Expected: HTTP 200, {\"status\":\"ok\"}."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Ingest",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Ingest - Happy Path (sysmon_demo.evtx)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Select data/sample_logs/sysmon_demo.evtx from the repo."
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/ingest",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "ingest"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Needs live Postgres (docker compose up -d db + alembic upgrade head). Expected: HTTP 200 with records_read/events_ingested/rule_matches/alerts_created/incident_ids fields. Without Postgres running, the Day 12 error handler now returns a clean HTTP 500 {\"detail\":\"internal server error\"} instead of a raw traceback -- see guide Section 19.6."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Ingest - Wrong File Type (expect 400)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Select any non-.evtx file, e.g. README.md."
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/ingest",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "ingest"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No DB needed -- this is pure validation before any DB call. Expected: HTTP 400, detail starts with \"unsupported file type: expected '.evtx'\"."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Ingest - Empty File (expect 400)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Select a 0-byte file named anything.evtx (create one with: New-Item empty.evtx -ItemType File)."
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/ingest",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "ingest"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No DB needed. Expected: HTTP 400, detail: \"uploaded file is empty\"."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Ingest - Malformed EVTX (expect 400)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Select a file with a .evtx extension but garbage content (e.g. rename a .txt with a few random bytes to garbage.evtx)."
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/ingest",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "ingest"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No DB needed -- fails during EVTX parsing before any DB call. Expected: HTTP 400, detail starts with \"failed to parse EVTX file:\"."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "MITRE",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List MITRE Techniques",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/mitre/techniques",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "mitre",
                "techniques"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No DB needed (reads the cached local MITRE dataset). Expected: HTTP 200, {\"techniques\":[...],\"count\":858}."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Incidents",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List Incidents - All",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "incidents"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Needs live Postgres. Expected: HTTP 200, {\"incidents\":[...],\"count\":N}, newest first."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List Incidents - Paginated (limit=1, offset=0)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents?limit=1&offset=0",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "incidents"
              ],
              "query": [
                { "key": "limit", "value": "1" },
                { "key": "offset", "value": "0" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Day 13 pagination. Needs live Postgres with more than one incident. Expected: HTTP 200, {\"incidents\":[...1 item...],\"count\":1,\"total\":N,\"limit\":1,\"offset\":0} -- total is the grand match count across all pages, count is just this page's size. Bump offset to 1, 2, ... to page through the rest; total stays the same each time."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List Incidents - Limit Above Cap (expect 422)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents?limit=500",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "incidents"
              ],
              "query": [
                { "key": "limit", "value": "500" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Day 13 pagination validation. No DB call reached -- FastAPI/pydantic rejects limit>200 before the route body runs. Expected: HTTP 422 with a validation error detail. Try offset=-1 instead of limit=500 for the negative-offset case -- same 422 behavior."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List Incidents - Filter by Severity",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents?severity=high",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "incidents"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "severity",
                  "value": "high"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Needs live Postgres. Edit the severity value to match a real incident (informational/low/medium/high/critical). Expected: HTTP 200, count reflects only matching-severity incidents."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List Incidents - Filter by Status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents?status=open",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "incidents"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "open"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Needs live Postgres. Expected: HTTP 200, count reflects only matching-status incidents."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List Incidents - Filter by Date Range",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents?start_date=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&end_date=2026-12-31T23:59:59Z",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "incidents"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "start_date",
                  "value": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"
                },
                {
                  "key": "end_date",
                  "value": "2026-12-31T23:59:59Z"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Needs live Postgres. ISO-8601 datetimes, filters on Incident.created_at. Expected: HTTP 200."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Incident Detail",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents/{{incident_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "incidents",
                "{{incident_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Needs live Postgres, and incident_id must be a real id (from an earlier Ingest or List Incidents response -- update the incident_id collection/environment variable). Expected: HTTP 200 with id/title/status/severity/host/created_at/mitre_technique_ids/techniques[]/alerts[] (each alert nests its event)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Incident Detail - 404",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents/999999",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "incidents",
                "999999"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Needs live Postgres (a reachable DB is required to determine the id doesn't exist). Expected: HTTP 404, {\"detail\":\"incident 999999 not found\"}."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Explain",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Explain Incident",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents/{{incident_id}}/explain",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "incidents",
                "{{incident_id}}",
                "explain"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Needs live Postgres, a real incident_id, and a real LLM_API_KEY in backend .env (2 live Gemini calls per request -- mind the free-tier daily quota, see guide Section 17.3/Troubleshooting). Expected: HTTP 200 with explanation/recommended_response/sources[]."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Chat",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Chat With Incident",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Why was this flagged?\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents/{{incident_id}}/chat",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "incidents",
                "{{incident_id}}",
                "chat"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Needs live Postgres, a real incident_id, and a real LLM_API_KEY (or GROQ_API_KEY) in backend .env (1 live LLM call per request -- mind the free-tier daily quota, see guide Section 21). Each call persists both the user message and the assistant reply as chat_messages rows, so retrieval scoped to this incident's context sees prior turns on the next call. Expected: HTTP 200 with incident_id/role (\"assistant\")/content/sources[]."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Chat With Incident - 404",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"hello\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/incidents/999999/chat",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "incidents",
                "999999",
                "chat"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Needs live Postgres (a reachable DB is required to determine the id doesn't exist). Expected: HTTP 404, {\"detail\":\"incident 999999 not found\"}."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
